jobs.description:
In line with our expectations, we expect our team members to be passionate about their work, to act with honesty and integrity, and to have a healthy dose of enthusiasm. The desired skills for the Quality Control Employee are also:
*  At least MBO level of working and thinking;
* 2-3 years work experience as a Quality Control Employee in a food company;
* Flexibility: working in four overlapping shifts, with Saturdays occasionally forming part of the working week;
* Fluency in spoken and written English; Dutch is an advantage;
* Knowledge of HACCP and GFSI;
* Strong communication skills, persuasive and decisive;
* Works accurately and is proactive;
* You are proficient in Excel and Word.

The New Plant - At The New Plant we produce Beyond Meats plant-based protein products for customers in Europe, the middle East and parts of Africa. Beyond Meat has been partnering with McDonalds sinds 2021 and supplies the vegetarian patty for the McPlant. Within your team, you will be working alongside three Quality Control Employee, a Quality Control Supervisor and a Quality Control Manager, and you will collaborate with two Quality Assurance Assistants.

Are you a natural leader with experience in logistics? Do you enjoy managing people while continuously improving operational processes? Then this could be the perfect opportunity for you!

We are looking for a Warehouse Supervisor to join an international logistics organization. In this role, you will be responsible for the daily warehouse operation, ensuring your team works safely, efficiently, and delivers the highest quality standards.

What will you do?
As a Warehouse Supervisor, you will lead a team of approximately 15 to 30 warehouse employees and temporary staff. You will be actively present on the warehouse floor and ensure that daily operations run smoothly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Coordinating inbound, storage, and outbound logistics activities;
- Leading, coaching, and motivating warehouse employees;
- Monitoring productivity, planning, and operational quality;
- Ensuring accurate administrative processing within the Warehouse Management System (WMS);
- Identifying operational bottlenecks and driving process improvements;
- Ensuring compliance with safety, quality, and company procedures;
- Conducting performance reviews, coaching sessions, and absence management;
- Working closely with Customer Service and the Warehouse Manager to continuously improve customer satisfaction.

You are a hands-on and motivated supervisor who knows how to inspire a team while maintaining focus on operational excellence.

You also have:

- An MBO Level 4 qualification, preferably in Logistics or Supply Chain;
- At least 2 years of leadership experience within a logistics or production environment;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Strong communication and leadership skills;
- Experience with warehouse operations and WMS systems;
- You can provide a valid Certificate of Conduct (VOG). If your VOG is approved, Olympia will reimburse the cost of €41.35. If your VOG is not approved, the cost will be at your own expense.
- You have your own accommodation;

As an Operator, you play a key role in the production process! Your goal is to ensure that production runs smoothly in either the Filet Americain or the slicing department. You will work alongside several colleagues in a dynamic production environment.

To give you a better idea of your future role, here is a selection of your daily responsibilities:

- Setting up and operating machines while ensuring they run without interruptions;
- Identifying and resolving machine malfunctions as quickly as possible;
- Converting machines for different production runs and performing routine maintenance checks;
- Operating the labeling line;
- Replacing labels when needed;
- Carrying out packing activities;Performing cleaning and housekeeping tasks.

Working hoursYour new job is scheduled from Monday to Friday, giving you the weekends off. Your workday starts at 6:30 AM and ends when the day's production has been completed.

- Experience as a Machine Operator, Line Operator, Mechanic, or someone who enjoys working on scooters or cars in their spare time and has a strong technical mindset;
- Willingness to work in  a day shift;
- Available full-time (40 hours per week);
- Good command of Dutch or English;
- Own transportation to travel to the work location;
- Living in the region of Zevenhuizen, Zoetermeer, The Hague, Bleiswijk, Rotterdam, Gouda, Waddinxveen, or nearby towns and cities.
